WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.320
The Marvel Cinematic Universe&nbsp;
just got a whole lot… smaller.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:09.000
The release of the first full trailer for&nbsp;
"Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania" is here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.080
but say goodbye to that lighthearted&nbsp;
tone from the first two Ant-Man movies.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:20.160
Starring Paul Rudd as Scott Lang, aka Ant-Man, and&nbsp;
Evangeline Lilly as Hope Van Dyne, aka the Wasp,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.840
this latest entry in the MCU depicts the&nbsp;
size-shifting team returning to the Quantum&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:29.640
Realm after Cassie Lang accidentally opens&nbsp;
a rift to the realm and drags them all in.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:36.743
"Wait – wait a minute. You're sending a signal&nbsp;
down to the Quantum Realm. Turn it off."

00:00:36.743 --> 00:00:42.300
Also along for the ride are the previous Ant-Man&nbsp;
and the Wasp, Dr. Hank Pym and Janet Van Dyne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:46.260
both of whom are probably dreaming of&nbsp;
superhero retirement by this point.

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:49.980
Unfortunately for our heroes, it&nbsp;
seems as though the Quantum Zone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.940
has its own array of inhabitants,&nbsp;
including Bill Murray — whose role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:59.400
is as yet a mystery — and a variant of Kang&nbsp;
the Conqueror, the MCU's newest big baddie.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:03.840
Oh, a quick aside, we're calling him a&nbsp;
"variant" because Kang's whole deal is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:08.640
that the Marvel multiverse is drowning in&nbsp;
Kangs, almost all of whom seem to be a kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:13.140
of tyrannical warlord. Before this trailer,&nbsp;
we'd only seen Kang in the Disney+ series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:17.400
"Loki," where the variant was a relatively&nbsp;
peaceful fellow at the end of the world.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:22.320
Now, with "Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania"&nbsp;
showcasing just how intimidating Kang the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:27.120
Conqueror can truly be, fans are eager to share&nbsp;
their opinions about the green-clad menace.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.360
One user reacted to the&nbsp;
trailer on Twitter by saying,

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:36.540
"CGI is on point. Also, Kang looks sick,&nbsp;
can't wait to see him pulverize Ant-Man!"

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:40.080
Another poster, charmingly&nbsp;
hopeful, responded by saying,

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.240
"Kang is gonna be the best marvel villain."

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:47.460
Less hopeful, another user retweeted the new&nbsp;
poster for "Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:52.320
which depicts Kang holding the tiny heroes atop&nbsp;
his middle finger like bread crumbs, saying,

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:56.015
"I've got a horrible feeling&nbsp;
Kang is going to K-word Scott."

00:01:56.242 --> 00:02:01.942
"Kill! … YES!"

00:02:01.942 --> 00:02:02.580
That's actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:06.960
a pretty common theory, by the way. The notion&nbsp;
that Kang will be this brutally merciless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.940
killer is so prevalent that some outlets have&nbsp;
practically pre-written obituaries for Scott Lang.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:17.040
It wouldn't be out of nowhere. Every time a&nbsp;
new major villain is introduced in the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:20.880
they have to make a noticeable first&nbsp;
impression somehow. For comparison,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:26.520
the mad titan Thanos killed Loki and Heimdall&nbsp;
in his first bout against the Avengers. There's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:30.540
just no way that everyone in "Ant-Man and the&nbsp;
Wasp: Quantumania" is making it out alive.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:35.820
One Twitter user predicted an entire multi-movie&nbsp;
arc for the conflict with Kang, saying,

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:40.680
"I can see every movie Kang is in, ending with&nbsp;
some sort of defeat, and then another Kang&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:46.320
variant just poppin in and they back to square one&nbsp;
[...] That would be sick. A never ending cycle."

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.114
"Feels like a fresh start."

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:53.160
A recent feature from Men's Health gives&nbsp;
us a pretty good look at the mentality that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:57.480
Jonathon Majors is taking in his approach&nbsp;
to portraying Kang. The interview reminds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:00.660
us that Majors is well-known for&nbsp;
immersing himself within a role,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:05.160
bringing both an intense work ethic and&nbsp;
even more intense energy to his work.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.860
When discussing his all-in approach, Majors said,

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:12.120
"I have a tremendous amount of faith in my&nbsp;
preparation and faith in something greater&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:15.780
than me ... And not because my ego&nbsp;
tells me I am but because I’m ready."

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:18.600
Crucially for a superhero movie, he boasted,

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:20.280
"I know I can take my shirt off."

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:24.960
The actor went on to describe how he'd&nbsp;
run countless miles, abstained from carbs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:30.120
and put his body on the line honing his physique&nbsp;
to the bare minimum of what comic book audiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:33.960
expect of their fearsome villains. He&nbsp;
also discussed how he worked with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:37.980
strength conditioning coach specifically&nbsp;
to create an "imposing figure" for Kang.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:43.200
Already there's at least one major movie on the&nbsp;
horizon set to center on Kang after "Ant-Man and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:48.420
the Wasp: Quantumania." With the help of Majors&nbsp;
and his fitness coaches, we're sure audiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:53.100
will be gladly fearing all the variations&nbsp;
of this imposing figure for years to come.

